      "writtenOn": "2025-03-07T10:21:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e AFAICT, the default implement is Predicate? All Matchable implementations subclass Predicate.\n\nIt\u0027s a weird class structure. Most classes here end up as `extend Predicate implements Matchable` to make sure they implement both. But the Predicate doesn\u0027t implement methods of Matchable (ie. match() ). So adding matchResult to it would be inconsistent",
      "parentUuid": "d22c3679_4c23ecef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 36
